A filter writes the sum of the three-by-three block around a cell, but only where the whole block fits inside the grid. What does this program print?

import java.util.Arrays;

public class A23 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] g = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}, {7, 8, 9}};
        int rows = 3;
        int cols = 3;
        int[][] out = new int[rows][cols];
        for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
                if (r > 0 && r + 1 < rows && c > 0 && c + 1 < cols) {
                    int sum = 0;
                    for (int dr = -1; dr <= 1; dr++) {
                        for (int dc = -1; dc <= 1; dc++) {
                            sum += g[r + dr][c + dc];
                        }
                    }
                    out[r][c] = sum;
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println(Arrays.deepToString(out));
    }
}

Three rows of different lengths are summed a column at a time, with the column bound taken from whichever row is shortest. What does this program print?

public class A24 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
